    "final_answer": "I've successfully found the ArXiv submission guidelines for figure formats. Here's the information:\n\n## ArXiv Submission Guidelines: Formats for Figures\n\n**Accepted figure formats:**\n\n1. **PostScript (PS, EPS)** — requires LaTeX processing\n2. **JPEG, GIF, PNG, or PDF figures** — requires PDFLaTeX processing\n\n**Important notes from ArXiv:**\n\n- ArXiv does **not accept submissions with omitted figures**, even if you provide links to view figures externally.\n- If you submit figures with your (La)TeX source, you should use standard macro packages (e.g., the `graphics` and `graphicx` packages) to have figures appear in the document.\n- ArXiv administration cannot provide help with TeX-related issues.\n- File names and extensions are **case sensitive** on their system (e.g., `Figure1.PDF` and `figure1.pdf` are different files).\n- Only these characters are accepted in file names: `a-z A-Z 0-9 _ + - . , =`\n\nFor complete context, the accepted submission formats in order of preference are:\n1. (La)TeX, AMS(La)TeX, PDFLaTeX\n2. PDF\n3. HTML with JPEG/PNG/GIF images\n\nArXiv does **not accept**: dvi, PS, or PDF created from TeX/LaTeX source, and they do not accept scanned documents, regardless of format.\n\nSource: https://info.arxiv.org/help/submit/figures.html",
